{
  "dom_id": "step-q61898",
  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "The standard form of the polynomial $2+3{x}^{2}+4{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}$ is",
  "worked_solution": "First, we collect like terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2+3{x}^{2}+4{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-{x}^{3} & = \\\\ 2+(3{x}^{2}-{x}^{2})+(4{x}^{3}-{x}^{3}) & = \\\\ 2+(3-1){x}^{2}+(4-1){x}^{3} & = \\\\ 2+2{x}^{2}+3{x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to express our polynomial in standard form.\n\nThe highest exponent term is $3{x}^{3},$ followed by $2{x}^{2},$ and finally $2.$\n\nSo, the standard form of the polynomial is:\n\n$$\n3{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+2\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
